In a #3-quart heavy saucepan{} on low heat, add @sugar{2 1/2%cups}, @flour{6%tablespoons} and @salt{pinch}. Pour in @evaporated milk{24%ounces} and stir constantly. The mixture will thicken slowly, about ~{15%minutes}.

Lightly beat @eggs{4%large}(yolks) in a medium size bowl. Add a ladleful of the thickened milk mixture to the eggs and whisk, to temper the eggs. Add the egg mixture into the saucepan and continue to whisk and cook until incorporated, roughly ~{2-3%minutes}.

Remove the saucepan from the heat and stir in @butter{1/2%stick}(cubed) and @vanilla extract{1%teaspoon}. Place the pudding into a bowl and cover with plastic wrap. Let cool in refrigerator for ~{150%minutes}.

Into a large bowl or trifle dish, add a layer of @vanilla wafers{1%box}, a layer of @bananas{5}(sliced), and top with pudding. Add @whipped cream{} and then repeat the layers. Garnish with crumbled cookies on top.